# A card exiled face down has no characteristics (CR 406.3a), so it has no mana cost and its mana value is 0 to anything
# that reads cards in exile. Bot1 foretells Delayed Blast Fireball (mana value 3) on turn 1, exiling it face down, then
# casts Ulamog, the Defiler, whose cast trigger has Bot2 exile the top half of its six-card library face up: Counterspell
# (mana value 2) and two Plains. Ulamog enters with counters equal to the greatest mana value among cards in exile: the
# face-up Counterspell's 2, not the face-down Fireball's 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Delayed Blast Fireball
Ulamog, the Defiler
Black Lotus x4
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x7
Counterspell
Plains x5

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Delayed Blast Fireball.Foretell
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
? Exile.FaceDown = Delayed Blast Fireball
Bot1.Hand.Ulamog, the Defiler.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = (face down); Counterspell; Plains; Plains
Exile.FaceDown = Delayed Blast Fireball
Bot1.Battlefield.Ulamog, the Defiler.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
